      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please see the inline comment on `test/kb_scan.c` to tighten the test assertion and simplify the test setup.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** ✅ Simulates holding the power button while `KEYBOARD_ROW_REFRESH` is asserted across all columns at runtime and verifies that `keyboard_scan_task` does not livelock between wait mode and poll mode.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Fits cleanly into `test/kb_scan.c` alongside `power_button_mask_test` in `run_test_step1()`.\n* **Code Simplicity:** ❌ `power_button_held_no_livelock_test()` can be simplified by asserting `raw_read_all_count` before cleanup (eliminating the temporary `reads` variable), using `memset(mock_state, BIT(KEYBOARD_ROW_REFRESH), sizeof(mock_state))` instead of a manual column loop, and removing the redundant `task_wake(TASK_ID_KEYSCAN)` call immediately after `reset_key_state()`.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ❌ Replace the magic `300` ms sleep duration and `10` read-count threshold with `crec_usleep(3 * keyscan_config.poll_timeout_us)` and an exact equality check (`TEST_EQ(raw_read_all_count, 1, \"%d\")`).\n* **Security:** ✅ No security concerns.\n* **Testing:** ❌ `TEST_LE(reads, 10, \"%d\")` is a weak inequality oracle that passes even when `reads \u003d\u003d 0` (the initial state of `raw_read_all_count`). Because `read_matrix(new_state, false)` does not mask `KEYBOARD_ROW_REFRESH` at runtime (`at_boot \u003d\u003d false`), `keyboard_scan_task` wakes from wait mode once (`raw_read_all_count \u003d\u003d 1`) and stays in poll mode sleeping between scans; please assert `TEST_EQ(raw_read_all_count, 1, \"%d\")`.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: S (+40, -0)`. Single, self-contained logical change adding a regression test for commit `9e6f494d76`.\n* **Commit Message:** ✅ Clear, accurate, and properly formatted with `BUG\u003d` and `TEST\u003d` tags. [🔗](http://go/tj/9eb2e5bb-14ba-4e1d-a34d-c628e928e6de)",
