      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Please tighten the assertion and simplify `power_button_held_no_livelock_test`:\n\n1. **Assert the exact expected wait-mode read count (`TEST_EQ(raw_read_all_count, 1, \"%d\")`) before cleanup:**\n   * Because `raw_read_all_count` is initialized to `0` on line 628, `TEST_LE(reads, 10, \"%d\")` would pass even if `keyboard_scan_task` never woke or never performed a wait-mode read (`reads \u003d\u003d 0`).\n   * With commit `9e6f494d76`, `read_matrix(new_state, false)` only clears `KEYBOARD_MASKED_BY_POWERBTN` when `at_boot` is `true`. At runtime (`at_boot \u003d\u003d false`), `read_matrix()` returns `1` (`pressed !\u003d 0`) on every poll scan while `KEYBOARD_ROW_REFRESH` is asserted across all columns, which continuously refreshes `poll_deadline` and keeps `keyboard_scan_task` in poll mode (sleeping between scans) without ever expiring `poll_timeout_us` or re-entering wait mode. Thus `raw_read_all_count` is deterministically `1` (the single wait-mode read when exiting `task_wait_event(-1)`).\n   * Checking `TEST_EQ(raw_read_all_count, 1, \"%d\")` before cleanup (matching `power_button_mask_test()` above) also eliminates the intermediate `reads` variable and the magic threshold `10`.\n2. **Use `memset` to assert the row across all columns:** Since `reset_key_state()` just zeroed `mock_state`, `memset(mock_state, BIT(KEYBOARD_ROW_REFRESH), sizeof(mock_state));` sets the row across all columns directly without the loop variable `c` or per-column `mock_key()` console spam.\n3. **Derive the sleep duration from `keyscan_config.poll_timeout_us` and drop the redundant `task_wake()`:** Use `crec_usleep(3 * keyscan_config.poll_timeout_us);` instead of the magic `300` ms literal, and remove `task_wake(TASK_ID_KEYSCAN);` on line 636 since `reset_key_state()` already wakes `TASK_ID_KEYSCAN` after clearing `mock_state`.\n\n```c\nstatic int power_button_held_no_livelock_test(void)\n{\n\t/*\n\t * Hold the power button with no other key pressed while the GSC\n\t * asserts the power-button-masked row on every column (Ti50 pass-\n\t * through / PWRBTN_ASSERTS_KSI3). The scan task must keep sleeping\n\t * between scans instead of bouncing between wait and poll modes,\n\t * otherwise lower priority tasks (HOOK_TICK -\u003e watchdog reload)\n\t * starve.\n\t */\n\tccprintf(\"\\nTest power button held, masked row on all columns.\\n\");\n\treset_key_state();\n\tcrec_msleep(40);\n\tpower_button_counter_divider \u003d 1;\n\tpower_button_counter \u003d 0;\n\tmemset(mock_state, BIT(KEYBOARD_ROW_REFRESH), sizeof(mock_state));\n\traw_read_all_count \u003d 0;\n\ttask_wake(TASK_ID_KEYSCAN);\n\tcrec_usleep(3 * keyscan_config.poll_timeout_us);\n\tccprintf(\"wait-mode row reads: %d\\n\", raw_read_all_count);\n\n\t/*\n\t * At runtime (at_boot \u003d\u003d false), read_matrix() does not mask\n\t * KEYBOARD_ROW_REFRESH, so keyboard_scan_task wakes from wait mode\n\t * once and remains in poll mode sleeping between scans.\n\t */\n\tTEST_EQ(raw_read_all_count, 1, \"%d\");\n\n\tpower_button_counter_divider \u003d 0;\n\treset_key_state();\n\tcrec_msleep(40);\n\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/9eb2e5bb-14ba-4e1d-a34d-c628e928e6de)",
